issue_context.body:
### Description

The repro case as-written, not using `PersistedAssemblyBuilder`, works correctly. But if you uncomment the alternative version that does use `PersistedAssemblyBuilder`, and comment out the normal `AssemblyBuilder` version, attempting to run it will throw `BadImageFormatException`.

### Reproduction Steps

```
using System.Reflection.Emit;
using System.Reflection;

namespace CorruptArrayEmit
{
	internal class EmitArray
	{
		static void Main()
		{
			try
			{
				var asm = Build();
				var type = asm.GetType("Foo")!;
				var method = type.GetMethod("Break")!;
				var result = method.Invoke(null, [type]);
				Console.WriteLine(result);
			}
			catch (Exception ex)
			{
				Console.WriteLine(ex.ToString());
			}
		}

		private static Assembly Build()
		{
			//var assemblyBuilder = new PersistedAssemblyBuilder(new("MyAssembly"), typeof(object).Assembly);
			var assemblyBuilder = AssemblyBuilder.DefineDynamicAssembly(new("MyAssembly"), AssemblyBuilderAccess.RunAndCollect);

			ModuleBuilder moduleBuilder = assemblyBuilder.DefineDynamicModule("MyAssembly");
			var typeBuilder = moduleBuilder.DefineType("Foo", TypeAttributes.Public, typeof(ValueType));
			typeBuilder.DefineDefaultConstructor(MethodAttributes.Public);

			var result = typeBuilder.DefineMethod("Break", MethodAttributes.Static | MethodAttributes.Public, typeof(bool), [typeof(object)]);
			var il = result.GetILGenerator();
			il.Emit(OpCodes.Ldarg_0);
			il.Emit(OpCodes.Isinst, typeBuilder.MakeArrayType());
			il.Emit(OpCodes.Ret);

			typeBuilder.CreateType();

			/*
			var filename = Path.GetFullPath(".\\MyAssembly.dll");
			assemblyBuilder.Save(filename);
			return Assembly.LoadFile(filename);
			*/
			return assemblyBuilder;
		}
	}
}
```

### Expected behavior

Both implementations should run successfully and write "False" to the terminal.

### Actual behavior

The `PersistedAssemblyBuilder` version of the code throws `BadImageFormatException`, with an error message indicating there's a problem with a type token.  ILDASM with Show Token Values enabled shows this:

```
.method /*06000002*/ public static bool  Break(object A_0) cil managed
{
  // Code size       7 (0x7)
  .maxstack  8
  IL_0000:  ldarg.0
  IL_0001:  isinst     valuetype [ERROR! NIL TOKEN][]/*1B000001*/
  IL_0006:  ret
} // end of method Foo::Break
```

### Regression?

This worked correctly when saving assemblies from Reflection.Emit in .NET Framework.

### Known Workarounds

_No response_

### Configuration

.NET 9, Preview 4
Windows 10, x64

